<p>The wind park runs nine 2.1 MW turbines and has averaged about a 27% capacity factor since 2009 on EIA's generation records, 25.5% in 2025; it is the only utility-scale wind generation in Utah County.<a class="fnref" href="#fs10"><sup>8</sup></a><a class="fnref" id="rs105" href="#fs105"><sup>91</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fd0"><sup>43</sup></a> <code>UPDATED</code> The solar park is UMPA's, sold to residents through the city's SharedSolar program and built on a closed landfill.<a class="fnref" href="#fs9"><sup>7</sup></a><a class="fnref" id="rs24" href="#fs24"><sup>21</sup></a><a class="fnref" id="rs25" href="#fs25"><sup>22</sup></a> The hydro plant sits on Powerhouse Road: three units under the Strawberry Water Users Association, the oldest in service since 1937.<a class="fnref" href="#fs8"><sup>6</sup></a><a class="fnref" id="rs26" href="#fs26"><sup>23</sup></a> Powerhouse Road serves the current warehouse site, and the city spent $220,000 straightening it for the roughly 60 trucks a day Fingerhut expected.<a class="fnref" id="rs19" href="#fs19"><sup>16</sup></a><a class="fnref" id="rs20" href="#fs20"><sup>17</sup></a> <code>UPDATED</code></p>
<p>Only one of those three supplies Spanish Fork customers: the 4.0 MW solar park.<a class="fnref" href="#fs9"><sup>7</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fs24"><sup>21</sup></a> The wind park sells to PacifiCorp under a 20-year agreement.<a class="fnref" href="#fs120"><sup>106</sup></a> The hydro plant is reported to sell to the South Utah Valley Electric Service District. <code>UNVERIFIED</code> Spanish Fork is not a Rocky Mountain Power city: it runs a municipal utility supplied wholesale by UMPA, whose largest single resource is market purchases, about 41% of its 2021 resource energy. <code>UPDATED</code><a class="fnref" href="#fs7"><sup>5</sup></a></p>
<p>Nameplate against nameplate, with no assumptions: Volition as proposed is 14.8× all 26.5 MW of existing city generation, and one facility at the 450 MW cap is 17.0×.<a class="fnref" href="#fs1"><sup>1</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fs10"><sup>8</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fs60"><sup>51</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fs116"><sup>102</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fd0"><sup>43</sup></a></p>
