  <h3 id="truck-traffic">Truck traffic</h3>
<p>Every truck figure below applies published ITE rates to the verified 1,054,000 sq ft: the weighted averages in ITE's 2016 high-cube warehouse study, and ITE manual rates as reproduced by two state transportation departments.<a class="fnref" href="#fs117"><sup>103</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fs88"><sup>41</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fs89"><sup>42</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fd0"><sup>43</sup></a> No traffic count for this building exists in any public record, so the figures describe a fully tenanted building, not present conditions. A trip end is one pass through the driveway: a truck arriving is one trip end, and the same truck leaving is another. <code>UPDATED</code> The only figures for today's use are the applicant's, and they disagree: 750 to 1,500 truck trips a month on its 18 AUG slides, 2,250 to 3,750 trucks a month on its 01 SEP slide. <code>APPLICANT ONLY</code><a class="fnref" href="#fs103"><sup>89</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fs91"><sup>77</sup></a></p>
<figure class="diagram">
    <div class="fig-t"><span class="fig-n">FIGURE 03</span>Truck trip ends per month: each warehouse use the zone allows, at its highest published rate, against the data center</div>
