<p><strong>And the handout's carbon figure is the permit's own.</strong><a class="fnref" href="#fs5"><sup>61</sup></a> <em>"Under 1.43M tons of CO2e a year at full build"</em> is the Intent to Approve's 1,434,855 tons rounded, though the permit figure is a little over 1.43 million rather than under it.<a class="fnref" href="#fs1"><sup>1</sup></a> Volition is publishing its own permit's potential-to-emit number, which is larger than this report's operating estimate of roughly 800,000 to 980,000 metric tons.<a class="fnref" href="#fd0"><sup>43</sup></a> <code>UPDATED</code> That estimate applies a 75% capacity factor to the proposed 393.25 MW nameplate, which is this report's assumption; the applicant's own 75% referred to the 250 MW it called the facility's maximum, and on that basis the datasheet rates give about 510,000 to 620,000 metric tons before cooling and conversion losses.<a class="fnref" href="#fs60"><sup>51</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fd0"><sup>43</sup></a> Both are correct at their stated basis. Quoting either without the basis is not.</p>
