<p><strong>$4B at the 2026 approved rate is $38.3M a year gross before depreciation, roughly $3.8M/year to Spanish Fork City</strong>, and about $37.1M in year one if all of it is generation equipment at 97% good. On the applicant's rounded $40M, the city's share is $4.0M.<a class="fnref" href="#fd0"><sup>43</sup></a> <code>UPDATED</code> (The 17 AUG edition applied the shares to the rounded $40M.) The rest is real public revenue and Nebo School District is a legitimate beneficiary. The 04 AUG presentation gave no city figure.<a class="fnref" href="#fs113"><sup>99</sup></a> The applicant's 18 AUG slides put about $4.0M a year to the city on a ~$44M total, which would need about $4.6B of taxable value, and its 01 SEP deck says most goes to Nebo schools.<a class="fnref" href="#fs103"><sup>89</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fs91"><sup>77</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fd0"><sup>43</sup></a> All of these figures are gross, before any community reinvestment rebate (§12).</p>
<p><strong>One commitment worth pinning down, from the video Volition played to Council on 04 AUG</strong> <code>APPLICANT ONLY</code><strong>:</strong> the minutes record the video as saying Volition would <em>"dedicate a portion of site revenues"</em> to the communities that host its facilities (packet p. 65).<a class="fnref" href="#fs60"><sup>51</sup></a> <code>UPDATED</code> A revenue share is stronger than a flat $500,000 floor, because a percentage scales with the facility and a flat figure does not. <strong>Ask which form the development agreement takes.</strong></p>
  <h3 id="the-tax-base-is-a-community-benefit-not-a-city-line-">The tax base is a community benefit, not a city line item</h3>
<p><strong>Nebo's share alone is nearly five times Spanish Fork City's entire annual property tax revenue from every parcel in the city, $5,885,340.</strong><a class="fnref" href="#fs68"><sup>59</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fd0"><sup>43</sup></a> <code>UPDATED</code> <strong>At 2018 to 2019 Utah high-school costs of $77.5M to $145M, that share alone would build one every three to five years</strong>.<a class="fnref" id="rs81" href="#fs81"><sup>74</sup></a> <strong>Nebo School District and Utah County have a direct and substantial interest here, and neither has appeared in the record.</strong></p>
