<p>All figures are in metric tons.<a class="fnref" href="#fd0"><sup>43</sup></a> <code>UPDATED</code> The applicant's own slide calls the two about the same per megawatt, the conservative end of this calculation.<a class="fnref" href="#fs1"><sup>1</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fs47"><sup>31</sup></a><a class="fnref" href="#fs103"><sup>89</sup></a> Both things are true at once: this adds roughly 886,000 metric tons of CO2 to Utah County that does not exist today, <em>and</em> it is the lowest-carbon way to run that compute given what actually gets built.<a class="fnref" href="#fd0"><sup>43</sup></a> Telling a council it equals four trucks throws away a real advantage.</p>
