  <li><strong>Carbon:</strong> gas engines emit 0.438 metric t/MWh, not 0.483 short, so Bloom is about 22% cleaner at its midpoint, not 29%; the "three or four trucks" claim fails on total CO2 by 2,060 to 2,750×, an understatement the applicant conceded on 18 AUG; the criteria-pollutant CO2-equivalent reading is withdrawn; upstream methane and the coal bar, now EIA's 1.048, are restated (§15, §23).</li>
